      "writtenOn": "2025-05-28T21:26:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t this be `if (count)`? `!count` means it\u0027s getting the descriptors which does transfer ownership of the rx buffer.",
      "revId": "d144c7c1855f43fd12a95ea61ad33e1a2d319f27",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4fd68666_109a9f14",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1118,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-28T21:49:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does the spec allow returning 0 here at all? It says INVALID_PARAMETERS means Unrecognized UUID in the FFA_ERROR encoding and it says one or more partition information descriptors` are returned in the RX buffer.",
      "parentUuid": "1a7d48f5_1167e019",
      "revId": "d144c7c1855f43fd12a95ea61ad33e1a2d319f27",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "79f66fc7_be28e9aa",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1118,
      "author": {
        "id": 1809582
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-28T22:09:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e uint32 Count w2\n• If Bit[0] \u003d b’0 in the Flags input parameter, this field contains the count of partition information descriptors corresponding to the specified UUID in w1-w4. The descriptors are populated in the RX buffer of the caller.\n• If Bit[0] \u003d b’1 in the Flags input parameter, this field contains the count of partitions deployed in the system corresponding to the specified UUID in w1-w4.\n\nIn either case, `count \u003d\u003d res-\u003ea2 \u003d\u003d 0` means that there are no descriptors in the buffer. The spec doesn\u0027t say what happens to the RX buffer in that case, but all current implementations skip the transfer.",
      "parentUuid": "1a7d48f5_1167e019",
      "revId": "d144c7c1855f43fd12a95ea61ad33e1a2d319f27",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dddd74e8_6808686d",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1118,
      "author": {
        "id": 1807569
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-28T22:20:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As Andrei said, this is the case where the call succeeded with zero descriptors in the rx buffer. ARM has indicated that the release of the spec will clarify that there is no transfer of ownership of the rx buffer when \n- count (`w2`) is zero.\n- Bit[0] \u003d b’1 in the Flags input parameter.\n\nThis lines up with the comments added in this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "79f66fc7_be28e9aa",
      "revId": "d144c7c1855f43fd12a95ea61ad33e1a2d319f27",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "06c3a301_a583a0be",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1118,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-28T22:30:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How can you have a result with zero descriptors in the RX buffer if you passed a valid UUID?",
      "parentUuid": "dddd74e8_6808686d",
      "revId": "d144c7c1855f43fd12a95ea61ad33e1a2d319f27",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ea9f4784_fbbe3d58",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1118,
      "author": {
        "id": 1807569
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-28T23:56:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking at Table 6.3 (FF-A 1.3 ALP0), if the SPM is the caller and a hypervisor is the caller, then there are no partitions available for discovery. So in that case, it sounds spec-compliant to have the call succeed and return a count of zero.\n\nIn this case (Hypervisor calls SPM), I don\u0027t know how the count could come back non-zero given that the Nil UUID case must include the caller and non-Nil UUID cases must return `INVALID_PARAMETERS` if UUID wasn\u0027t recognized.\n\nI checked the EL3 SPMC in ATF and it will indeed return `FFA_ERROR`/`INVALID_PARAMETERS` if count is zero.\n\nI could open a follow-up CL to discuss whether we should `WARN_ON` a zero count. WDYT @arve@android.com?",
      "parentUuid": "06c3a301_a583a0be",
      "revId": "d144c7c1855f43fd12a95ea61ad33e1a2d319f27",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8852c62b_b56b55ca",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
